  "english": "23. Sunday. Tone 4 [Bk - Second Plagal]. Fifth [Sunday]. Father of all [Harts] Tone 6 [Gk]: \"Before all eternity\" (Nakhayavitean). Evening Dismissal [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [Bk]: \"From the morning\" (Arravotean) to the end.\n24. Monday. Tone 3 [Gj]. David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n29. Saturday. Tone 2 [Ak]. Sons of Thunder. Feast-breath [Barekendan] of the Fast of the Nativity.\n30. Sunday. Tone 3 [Dz]. Sixth [Sunday]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. Evening Dismissal [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [Dz]: \"Today they rejoiced\" (Aysor zuarchatsan) to the end.\n31. Monday. Tone 4 [Bk]. Fast. Father of all [Harts] Tone 6 [Gk]: \"Blessed is God, blessed\" (Orhneal er astuats orhneal).\n\nIn January:\n5. Saturday. Tone 1 [Aj]. Vigil [Chragaloyts] of the Nativity of Christ.\n\nTHE SEVEN-DAY CYCLE OF THE ROMANS 7.\n\nFebruary:\n6. Monday. The Atovmian Saints, and Bishop Mark, Priest Pionius, and others.\n13. Monday. The Ghevondian Saints.\n14. Tuesday. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarrnyndarrach].\n19. Sunday. Tone 8 [Dk]. Great Barekendan [Great Lent]. See also the others according to their order in the First Volume.\n\nApril:\n7. Friday. Tone 4 [Dj]. Great Friday [Holy Friday], and the Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\n9. Sunday. Tone 1 [Aj]. Easter [Zatik]. Day of the Resurrection of Christ. See according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nMay:\nA.......H.H.Dz [Tone marker/Rubric]\n18. Thursday. Tone 8 [Dk]. Ascension of Christ.\n28. Sunday. Tone 2 [Ak]. Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. Feast-breath [Barekendan] of the Elijah Fast.\n\nIn June:\n4. Sunday. Tone 1 [Aj]. First [Sunday]. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Father of all [Harts] Tone 1 [Adz]: \"Who came for the salvation of the universe\" (Or ekir i prkutiun tiezerats).\n\nIn July:\n16. Sunday. Tone 3 [Dz]. Transfiguration [Vartavar]. The season of non-fasting days [utik] is fourteen days.\n\nIn January:\n6. FRIDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The season of non-fasting days [utik] is fourteen days.\n14. Saturday. John the Forerunner [Karapet].\n15. Sunday. First [Sunday]. Father of all [Harts] Tone 8 [Ddz]: \"The dawning of the Only-Begotten\" (Tsagumn miatsni).\n16. Monday. Patriarch Peter, Blaise, and others.\n17. Tuesday. Anthony, and Tryphon, Barsauma, and Onuphrius.\n19. Thursday. King Theodosius, and the Holy Children of Ephesus.\n21. Saturday. Patriarchs Athanasius and Cyril.\n22. Sunday. Second [Sunday]. Father of all [Harts] Tone 6 [Gk]: \"Today He put on\" (Aysor zgetsa).\n23. Monday. Cyriacus and Julitta, and Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Gregory.\n24. Tuesday. Vahan of Goghtn, and Eugénie the Virgin, and others.\n26. Thursday. Eugene, Macarius, etc.\n28. Saturday. Gregory the Theologian.\n29. Sunday. Third [Sunday]. Feast-breath [Barekendan] of the Fast of the Catechumens. And see the rest in the First Volume up to Transfiguration [Vartavar], keeping the order of this place.",
